  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_constituencies_of_the_Andhra_Pradesh_Legislative_Assembly (district column = current districts incl. the 31 Dec 2025 changes; table cites the 2008 Delimitation Order, Andhra Pradesh Gazette pp. 7-15; raw wikitext read 2026-10-06)",
  "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_constituencies_of_the_Andhra_Pradesh_Legislative_Assembly&oldid=1057052287 (25 Nov 2021 revision, before the 2022 reorganisation: each seat's old (13-district) district; used for seatRegions)",
  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_districts_of_Andhra_Pradesh (28 districts: 26 from 4 April 2022 + Markapuram and Polavaram from 31 December 2025; Annamayya HQ moved Rayachoti -> Madanapalle; cites Eenadu 30 Dec 2025 and The Hindu 4 Apr 2022)",
  "https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2025/Dec/30/andhra-pradesh-cabinet-approves-formation-of-two-new-districts (cited by Wikipedia's Markapuram district page)",
  "https://www.thehansindia.com/andhra-pradesh/madanapalle-becomes-district-headquarters-from-today-1035505 (2025 changes: Rajampet back to YSR Kadapa, Kodur to Tirupati, Punganur to Annamayya; cited by Wikipedia's Annamayya district page)",
  "Wikipedia district pages (all 28; raw wikitext read 2026-10-06) for cross-checking each district's assembly segments and mandal lists, notably East Godavari (Mandapeta), Tirupati / Nellore (Venkatagiri), Tirupati / Chittoor (Nagari), Annamayya / Chittoor (Punganur), Visakhapatnam / Anakapalli (Pendurthi), Krishna / NTR (Gannavaram), West Godavari / Eluru (Unguturu)"
 ],
 "notes": "Districts are the 28 current districts: the 26 of the 4 April 2022 reorganisation plus Markapuram (from Prakasam: Yerragondapalem, Markapuram, Giddalur, Kanigiri) and Polavaram (from Alluri Sitharama Raju: Rampachodavaram), formed 31 December 2025, when seats also moved: Addanki (Bapatla -> Prakasam), Kandukur (Nellore -> Prakasam), Gudur (Tirupati -> Nellore), Rajampet (Annamayya -> YSR Kadapa), Kodur (Annamayya -> Tirupati), Mandapeta (Konaseema -> East Godavari; Mandapeta and Kapileswarapuram mandals now in East Godavari, Alamuru in Konaseema - the Wikipedia constituency list still shows Konaseema, the East Godavari and Konaseema district pages show the move), and Punganur town to Annamayya. Seats split across two districts are placed in the district holding the seat's headquarters town and most of its mandals: Venkatagiri 122 -> Tirupati (Venkatagiri, Dakkili, Balayapalli; Kaluvoya, Rapur, Sydapuram are in Nellore); Nagari 170 -> Chittoor (Nagari, Nindra, Vijayapuram; Puttur, Vadamalapeta in Tirupati); Punganur 165 -> Annamayya (Punganur, Chowdepalle, Sodam, Somala; Pulicherla, Rompicherla in Chittoor); Pendurthi 31 -> Anakapalli (Sabbavaram, Paravada; Pendurthi mandal is in Visakhapatnam - follows the constituency list, least certain); Gannavaram 71 -> Krishna (Vijayawada Rural part in NTR); Unguturu 63 -> Eluru (Unguturu, Bhimadole, Nidamarru; Ganapavaram in West Godavari); Rampachodavaram 53 -> Polavaram; Gopalapuram 66 -> East Godavari (Dwaraka Tirumala in Eluru). Regions follow the 13 districts before 2022 (agreed with the user), so they are given per seat in seatRegions and regions list no districts (Tirupati spans two regions: Sullurpeta and Venkatagiri were old Nellore = Coastal, Kodur old Kadapa = Rayalaseema; Markapuram district is old Prakasam = Coastal although Wikipedia's region list now puts it under Rayalaseema). Old districts by seat number (2008 Delimitation Order order): Srikakulam 1-10, Vizianagaram 11-19, Visakhapatnam 20-34 (Uttarandhra, 34); East Godavari 35-53, West Godavari 54-68, Krishna 69-84, Guntur 85-101, Prakasam 102-113, Nellore 114-123 (Coastal Andhra, 89); YSR Kadapa 124-133, Kurnool 134-147, Anantapur 148-161, Chittoor 162-175 (Rayalaseema, 52).",
